  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 3.36,
      "text": "people who know AI best still don't know where it's actually going."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.14,
      "end": 5.34,
      "text": "This uncertainty isn't new."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.98,
      "end": 10.96,
      "text": "Every time a major technology arrives, the smartest people around make highly confident"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.96,
      "end": 14.54,
      "text": "predictions about it, and those predictions miss in both directions."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.18,
      "end": 20.58,
      "text": "In 1995, astronomer Clifford Stole predicted that online shopping could not compete with"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.58,
      "end": 20.78,
      "text": "malls."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.56,
      "end": 23.82,
      "text": "Today, it is a routine part of everyday life."
    },
    {
      "start": 23.82,
      "end": 30.02,
      "text": "And going back to 1940, Ford Motor Company founder Henry Ford predicted a flying car was"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.02,
      "end": 30.32,
      "text": "coming."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.88,
      "end": 33.42,
      "text": "We are still waiting for that to become ordinary transportation."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.1,
      "end": 37.9,
      "text": "A technology becomes the future only when people change their habits around it."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.46,
      "end": 39.4,
      "text": "Machines improve fast."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.06,
      "end": 41.26,
      "text": "Habits change at human speed."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.24,
      "end": 46.32,
      "text": "So looking at this board, here is the exact question worth asking."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.02,
      "end": 48.58,
      "text": "What is actually in your hands?"
    },
    {
      "start": 48.58,
      "end": 49.76,
      "text": "And what isn't?"
    }
  ],
